osine(34) in tRNA(Tyr) to form galactosyl-queuosine(34) (PubMed:37992713). Mannosylation of queuosine(34) in tRNA(Tyr) is required to slow-down elongation at cognate codons UAC and suppress stop codon readthrough, thereby regulating protein translation (PubMed:37992713)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}